          ":question/id": "35e39332-390d-57d5-8a71-b2e823ef2c1d",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-131713",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 4x-8y &=4 \\\\ -4x+8y &=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$  in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2y+1 \\\\ y &=y,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2y+1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
